title The sixth path, and the rule that was written inside it fifteen times
prompt Autonomous loop -- take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, close reds first, send each finished increment as its own signed round
think The ranked queue handed over suits_path at the head, tied at 350 with the mind_the_impasse lifted one lap earlier. Measured before cutting: declared=15 identical=15 lines=28 stub=3 fall=350 widens=0.
think Read the family before lifting it. suits_path is the sixth member of the reader-box path family -- hand_path, tell_path, renew_path, ask_path, found_path, suits_path -- five of which already stand lifted in caravan/ladder_checks.rye, and found_path stands directly above where this one belongs.
think The bodies are private fn rather than pub fn in all fifteen rungs, so the stubs keep that visibility and only the harness copy publishes. The lift widens nothing because every symbol the body reaches -- addressable, reader_dir, max_note_path_len, NoteError -- already stood public in all fifteen.
think Lifted into caravan/ladder_checks.rye as pub fn suits_path(comptime rung: type, buf: *[rung.max_note_path_len]u8, address: []const u8) rung.NoteError![]const u8, seated directly beneath found_path. All three asserts travelled, including the comptime assert(suffix.len == ".found".len).
think Carry 60,160 -> 59,810, a fall of 350 -- the scan's predicted number to the digit, nine laps running. Lowered the ceiling in tools/caravan_ladder_carry_witness.rish and the scan default together; the choir caught the second one when only the first had moved, which is the bijection doing its job.
think Rotated the pins: folded row to suits_path, queue head to hold_the_matter at 336, sink 65,420 -> 65,045 total and 64,280 -> 63,905 above the line, farewell holding 3,826 -> 3,801.
obs The finding worth carrying is that this family is held together by an assert rather than by a resemblance. The comptime assert(suffix.len == ".found".len) says a reader's word must land in the same box, at the same width, as the finding it answers. That is a real rule about the wire, and it stood written fifteen times -- fifteen files free to drift apart on a constraint that binds all of them. The five siblings lifted before it each carried the same shape of assert, which is why the family reads as one rule rather than six similar functions.
obs The second finding is smaller and worth naming anyway: two ceilings had to fall together, one in the witness and one in the scan default, and lowering only the witness left the scan blessing a number nobody had asserted. The suite caught it on the next run. A number written twice is a number that can disagree with itself, which is this whole arc's thesis pointed at its own meters.
